WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.320
Threat intelligence helps hunters decide where to focus.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:07.345
It provides context about adversary behaviors, affected sectors, common objectives,

00:00:07.345 --> 00:00:12.175
technology trends, and observed changes that may be relevant to the organization.

00:00:12.175 --> 00:00:15.798
Intelligence is most useful when connected to local risk.

00:00:15.798 --> 00:00:21.030
A report may be important globally but less relevant to the organization's technologies,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.445
geography, data, customers, or operating model.

00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:26.262
Hunters should evaluate applicability before committing resources.

00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:30.690
Behavioral information often has longer value than a single technical indicator.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.520
Understanding the kinds of actions an adversary may attempt can help teams

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.350
look for patterns across different systems even after specific infrastructure or identifiers

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.000
change.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.830
Technical indicators can still support focused review, but they require context, freshness,

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.635
and validation.

00:00:46.635 --> 00:00:52.672
An old or low-confidence indicator should not automatically be treated as proof of harmful activity.

00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:57.502
Intelligence can shape a hypothesis by identifying a plausible concern, likely targets,

00:00:57.502 --> 00:00:59.917
expected evidence, and relevant data sources.

00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:02.735
The resulting hunt should remain an investigation,

00:01:02.735 --> 00:01:06.357
not a predetermined effort to confirm the intelligence report.

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.370
Local observations also improve intelligence.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:13.602
Hunters may learn that a reported behavior is not visible with current telemetry,

00:01:13.602 --> 00:01:16.420
that it appears differently in their environment,

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:19.640
or that particular systems deserve stronger defensive attention.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.262
Collaboration among intelligence analysts, hunters, detection engineers, incident responders,

00:01:23.262 --> 00:01:26.482
and system owners creates a useful feedback loop.

00:01:26.482 --> 00:01:28.897
External context becomes a local question,

00:01:28.897 --> 00:01:31.715
and local evidence improves future defensive decisions.

00:01:31.715 --> 00:01:34.935
Intelligence does not guarantee findings or replace telemetry.

00:01:34.935 --> 00:01:39.765
It helps prioritize limited hunting capacity and gives analysts a stronger basis

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:43.140
for selecting questions that matter to the organization's risk.
